Subject: [PATCH] minimum arm64: ship R Chromium on the live image

build-renku-arm64-iso.sh now builds two variants from the same patched
tree: the USB install medium (unchanged -- 0041's post-install job fetches
R Chromium there, once a real install has network) and a live medium that
ships it already on the image, for running straight off the medium with
no install and no network wait -- what MacRenkuOS boots.

Adds `rchromium-154.0.8036.0-31` to the arm64 repository list, same as
`rappmarket-1.0.0-4` right above it, but only pulls it onto the image
(`AddHaikuImageSystemPackages rchromium`) when the build sets
`RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1` -- a jam variable the build script now passes with
`-s`, read here as `$(RENKU_LIVE_BUILD)`. The install variant (the
default) never requests it, so `AddRepositoryPackage`'s own silent-drop
behavior (see 0014's note on the same thing happening to openssl3) just
leaves it out of that build's local index; nothing needs its hpkg to be
present in download/ unless RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1 actually asks for it.

That hpkg needs re-vendoring before it can sit in this local HaikuPorts-
info repository at all: package_repo refuses a package whose vendor
differs from the rest of it, the same constraint 0012's curl/wget and
0020's rappmarket already hit, there worked around by rebuilding each one
from its own recipe with the vendor forced to "Haiku Project". Rebuilding
R Chromium from source the same way is a multi-hour native Chromium
build, so build-renku-arm64-iso.sh instead re-vendors the already-built
hpkg: extract it with the host `package` tool (built as `<build>package`,
the same way jam builds any other host-side tool it needs), edit the
vendor line in the `.PackageInfo` extraction writes out, and repack with
that edited copy -- same binaries, only the metadata differs.

diff --git a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
index ef9a358f..3549af50 100644
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
@@ -250,6 +250,18 @@ rule DefineDefaultBuildProfiles
 					;
 			}

+			# R Chromium: only for the live medium (RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1, set
+			# by build-renku-arm64-iso.sh), which ships it on the image
+			# instead of leaving it for 0041's post-install job to fetch.
+			# Needs the hpkg re-vendored to "Haiku Project" and staged into
+			# download/ first -- see build-renku-arm64-iso.sh's own
+			# "Staging R Chromium for the live image" step.
+			if $(TARGET_PACKAGING_ARCH) = arm64 && $(RENKU_LIVE_BUILD) = 1 {
+				AddHaikuImageSystemPackages
+					rchromium
+					;
+			}
+
 			# The image translators. The minimum profile ships STXTTranslator
 			# alone, so ShowImage opened nothing and a picture chosen as the
 			# desktop background was never drawn. JPEG, PNG, WebP and AVIF
diff --git a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64 b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
index d08dd60c..fb5ba78b 100644
--- a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
+++ b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
@@ -74,6 +74,10 @@ RemotePackageRepository HaikuPorts
 	openssh-10.4p1-1
 	# R AppMarket -- published in RENKU Apps, same as curl/gzip/tar/wget above.
 	rappmarket-1.0.0-4
+	# R Chromium -- published in RENKU Apps, re-vendored to "Haiku Project"
+	# at build time (see build-renku-arm64-iso.sh); only pulled onto the
+	# image when RENKU_LIVE_BUILD=1 (see DefaultBuildProfiles).
+	rchromium-154.0.8036.0-31
 	# The image translators, prebuilt against haikuwebkit's libjpeg-turbo,
 	# libpng and libwebp and libavif1.0's libavif (see DefaultBuildProfiles).
 	renku_imagetranslators-1.0.0-1
